\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces Two-way science links in LISA (upper) and miniLISA (lower). In LISA, the received laser field interferes with the local field after propagation between spacecraft. Optical sidebands carry the transmitting clock fluctuations, and the receiving clock references the phase measurement. In miniLISA, a common reference laser produces MHz input beat notes, and electronic delay lines reproduce the propagation and subtraction of remote and local signals. The lower-panel frequency and clock labels require the updates noted below.}}{3}{figure.1}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:armlink}{{1}{3}{Two-way science links in LISA (upper) and miniLISA (lower). In LISA, the received laser field interferes with the local field after propagation between spacecraft. Optical sidebands carry the transmitting clock fluctuations, and the receiving clock references the phase measurement. In miniLISA, a common reference laser produces MHz input beat notes, and electronic delay lines reproduce the propagation and subtraction of remote and local signals. The lower-panel frequency and clock labels require the updates noted below}{figure.1}{}}
